WEBVTT

00:00:00.261 --> 00:00:02.992
Last video ended here, with the integral from

00:00:03.052 --> 00:00:05.301
minus two to one, of x squared.

00:00:05.984 --> 00:00:08.631
The primitive is x cubed over three, so

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:11.801
we need one third, minus negative two cubed

00:00:11.923 --> 00:00:12.363
over three.

00:00:13.068 --> 00:00:14.980
It's like reading a thermometer on a frosty

00:00:15.021 --> 00:00:15.342
morning.

00:00:15.806 --> 00:00:18.270
The change is the later reading, minus the

00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:18.911
earlier one,

00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:21.236
and the earlier one can be below zero.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:23.713
Before we work it out, look at the

00:00:23.755 --> 00:00:24.056
graph.

00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:27.687
X squared is never negative, so every strip

00:00:27.788 --> 00:00:29.050
sits above the axis.

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:31.800
Should the answer be positive, or negative?

00:00:32.726 --> 00:00:34.438
Here's a slip that happens all the time.

00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:37.268
Negative two cubed is minus eight,

00:00:37.811 --> 00:00:40.719
and someone writes one third minus eight thirds,

00:00:41.181 --> 00:00:42.524
which is minus seven thirds.

00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:45.599
A negative answer, from a region that's all

00:00:45.761 --> 00:00:46.604
above the axis.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:48.395
Something has gone wrong.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.033
So how do we evaluate definite integrals without

00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:52.797
losing signs?

00:00:56.441 --> 00:00:58.549
The trouble is the second minus sign.

00:00:59.212 --> 00:01:00.003
Think of the thermometer.

00:01:00.632 --> 00:01:03.143
At six it read minus two degrees, and

00:01:03.164 --> 00:01:04.449
at nine it read one degree.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.123
It warmed by one, minus, bracket, minus two,

00:01:08.506 --> 00:01:11.054
which is three degrees, not one minus two.

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:13.733
F of a works the same way.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:16.062
F of a means the primitive at the

00:01:16.164 --> 00:01:17.587
lower limit, the start.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.592
Here that's F of minus two, which is

00:01:20.674 --> 00:01:23.417
minus eight thirds, a negative number, and the

00:01:23.478 --> 00:01:25.200
rule subtracts the whole of it.

00:01:25.882 --> 00:01:27.391
So put F of a in its own

00:01:27.452 --> 00:01:27.813
brackets,

00:01:28.377 --> 00:01:28.799
every time.

00:01:29.543 --> 00:01:32.499
One third, minus, bracket, minus eight thirds.

00:01:33.204 --> 00:01:34.730
Subtracting a negative adds,

00:01:35.233 --> 00:01:37.602
so that's one third plus eight thirds, which

00:01:37.643 --> 00:01:38.004
is three.

00:01:38.669 --> 00:01:39.939
Positive, as the picture said.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.573
The minus sign in the rule belongs to

00:01:42.614 --> 00:01:43.316
the subtraction.

00:01:43.819 --> 00:01:46.325
The minus sign inside F of a belongs

00:01:46.366 --> 00:01:46.927
to the number.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.397
Keep them apart, and neither gets lost.

00:01:50.141 --> 00:01:51.770
We can check that three another way.

00:01:52.415 --> 00:01:53.850
Split the region at zero.

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:57.037
From minus two to zero, the integral is

00:01:57.237 --> 00:02:00.963
zero, minus, bracket, minus eight thirds, which is

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:01.744
eight thirds.

00:02:02.386 --> 00:02:04.876
From zero to one, it's one third minus

00:02:04.937 --> 00:02:06.563
zero, which is one third.

00:02:07.288 --> 00:02:09.922
Eight thirds plus one third is three, the

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:10.424
same answer.

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:12.652
The thermometer does the same thing,

00:02:13.154 --> 00:02:15.599
two degrees up to zero, then one more.

00:02:16.322 --> 00:02:18.418
That always works, for a continuous function.

00:02:18.842 --> 00:02:20.865
The integral from a to b, plus the

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.209
integral from b to c, is the integral

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.313
from a to c, when b is between

00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:25.473
them.

00:02:26.115 --> 00:02:28.879
In primitives, that's F of b minus F

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.483
of a, plus F of c minus F

00:02:31.524 --> 00:02:31.824
of b.

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.857
The middle value cancels, so you're left with

00:02:35.079 --> 00:02:36.766
F of c minus F of a.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.715
On the graph, two regions side by side

00:02:39.856 --> 00:02:40.778
make one region.

00:02:41.428 --> 00:02:42.975
What if the limits come the other way

00:02:43.076 --> 00:02:45.607
round, from one down to minus two?

00:02:46.352 --> 00:02:48.141
The rule still says F of the top,

00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:49.327
minus F of the bottom.

00:02:50.031 --> 00:02:51.415
Now the top is minus two,

00:02:51.957 --> 00:02:54.765
so it's minus eight thirds, minus one third,

00:02:55.128 --> 00:02:56.090
which is minus three.

00:02:56.894 --> 00:02:59.002
Swapping the ends swaps the order of the

00:02:59.043 --> 00:03:01.392
subtraction, so the answer changes sign.

00:03:02.177 --> 00:03:04.523
On the thermometer, that's the evening, cooling from

00:03:04.705 --> 00:03:07.092
one degree back to minus two, a change

00:03:07.113 --> 00:03:07.894
of minus three.

00:03:08.718 --> 00:03:10.947
That's how a backwards integral is defined.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.021
The integral from b to a is minus

00:03:14.143 --> 00:03:15.529
the integral from a to b.

00:03:16.293 --> 00:03:18.700
Picture the strips running from right to left.

00:03:19.344 --> 00:03:22.057
Every strip's width is negative, so every strip

00:03:22.158 --> 00:03:22.961
flips its sign.

00:03:23.686 --> 00:03:25.373
And if both ends are the same, there

00:03:25.394 --> 00:03:27.262
are no strips at all, so the integral

00:03:27.343 --> 00:03:27.683
is zero.

00:03:28.768 --> 00:03:31.293
Signs get trickier when the primitive has a

00:03:31.394 --> 00:03:32.696
minus sign of its own.

00:03:33.499 --> 00:03:36.153
Find the integral from zero to pi, of

00:03:36.275 --> 00:03:36.817
sine x.

00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:39.387
A primitive is minus cos x.

00:03:40.232 --> 00:03:43.081
At pi, that's minus cos pi, which is

00:03:43.243 --> 00:03:45.570
minus, minus one, so it's one.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:48.738
At zero, it's minus cos zero,

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.202
which is minus one.

00:03:50.864 --> 00:03:54.331
So the answer is one, minus, bracket, minus

00:03:54.493 --> 00:03:55.734
one, which is two.

00:03:56.637 --> 00:03:58.720
Sine x is above the axis from zero

00:03:58.761 --> 00:04:01.285
to pi, so a positive answer is what

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:01.886
we expect.

00:04:02.749 --> 00:04:05.455
One minus one, giving zero, is the slip

00:04:05.596 --> 00:04:06.558
the brackets prevent.

00:04:07.382 --> 00:04:09.396
The same care works with an inside.

00:04:10.021 --> 00:04:12.204
The integral from zero to pi over four,

00:04:12.445 --> 00:04:15.289
of sine two x, has primitive minus a

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.651
half cos two x.

00:04:17.393 --> 00:04:19.558
At the top that's zero, and at the

00:04:19.619 --> 00:04:21.343
bottom it's minus a half.

00:04:21.865 --> 00:04:25.238
So the answer is zero, minus, bracket, minus

00:04:25.279 --> 00:04:26.845
a half, which is a half.

00:04:27.544 --> 00:04:28.799
Next, an exponential.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.768
Find the integral from zero to two, of

00:04:31.948 --> 00:04:33.472
e to the x, plus x.

00:04:34.174 --> 00:04:35.966
A primitive is e to the x, plus

00:04:36.147 --> 00:04:37.154
x squared over two.

00:04:37.957 --> 00:04:40.325
At two, that's e squared plus two.

00:04:40.967 --> 00:04:42.815
At zero, it's e to the zero plus

00:04:42.855 --> 00:04:45.023
zero, and e to the zero is one,

00:04:45.305 --> 00:04:45.807
not zero.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.293
So the answer is e squared plus two,

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.578
minus one, which is e squared plus one,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.481
about eight point three nine.

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:54.712
Logs go the other way.

00:04:55.215 --> 00:04:57.080
The integral from one to e, of one

00:04:57.141 --> 00:04:59.107
over x, is the natural log of e,

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.014
minus the natural log of one.

00:05:01.656 --> 00:05:03.761
The natural log of one is zero, so

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:04.885
that answer is just one.

00:05:05.788 --> 00:05:08.173
Leave answers exact, like e squared plus one,

00:05:08.495 --> 00:05:10.438
unless a question asks for a decimal.

00:05:11.017 --> 00:05:12.429
The rule also runs backwards.

00:05:13.015 --> 00:05:15.620
Find k, with k greater than one, so

00:05:15.641 --> 00:05:17.705
that the integral from one to k of

00:05:17.826 --> 00:05:19.128
two x equals eight.

00:05:20.012 --> 00:05:22.098
A primitive of two x is x squared,

00:05:22.461 --> 00:05:25.049
so the integral is k squared, minus one

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:25.390
squared.

00:05:25.995 --> 00:05:28.089
Set k squared minus one equal to eight.

00:05:28.573 --> 00:05:30.839
Then k squared is nine, so k is

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.444
three, or minus three.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:33.946
Now the sign check.

00:05:34.468 --> 00:05:36.934
Minus three fits the equation too, because the

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.441
integral from one down to minus three is

00:05:39.462 --> 00:05:41.507
a backwards integral, and it comes out as

00:05:41.588 --> 00:05:42.570
plus eight as well.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:43.956
But the question says k

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.131
is greater than one, so k equals three.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:48.837
Here's the line to remember.

00:05:49.526 --> 00:05:51.123
Top, minus bracketed bottom.

00:05:51.688 --> 00:05:53.157
Swap the ends, swap the sign.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:56.004
Split at a point inside, and the pieces

00:05:56.025 --> 00:05:56.425
add up.

00:05:59.063 --> 00:05:59.427
Your turn.

00:06:00.053 --> 00:06:03.046
Evaluate the integral from pi over three to

00:06:03.127 --> 00:06:04.814
pi, of sine x.

00:06:05.376 --> 00:06:06.319
Pause here to answer.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.584
A primitive is minus cos x.

00:06:19.351 --> 00:06:20.436
At pi, that's one.

00:06:21.363 --> 00:06:23.352
At pi over three, it's minus a half.

00:06:24.235 --> 00:06:24.955
So the answer is

00:06:25.516 --> 00:06:28.659
one, minus, bracket, minus a half, which is

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.360
three halves.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:31.198
A half is wrong.

00:06:31.704 --> 00:06:33.798
It drops the bracket, and subtracts a half

00:06:33.899 --> 00:06:34.644
instead of adding it.

00:06:36.286 --> 00:06:36.693
Last one.

00:06:37.545 --> 00:06:39.461
The function f is continuous.

00:06:40.044 --> 00:06:42.407
The integral from zero to five of f

00:06:42.588 --> 00:06:44.870
is seven, and the integral from zero to

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.372
two of f is three.

00:06:47.174 --> 00:06:49.308
Find the integral from five to two of

00:06:49.329 --> 00:06:49.369
f.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:51.715
Pause here to answer.

00:07:02.344 --> 00:07:03.295
Split at two.

00:07:04.182 --> 00:07:06.210
The integral from zero to two, plus the

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.720
integral from two to five, is the integral

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:09.824
from zero to five.

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:13.033
So three plus the unknown is seven,

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.519
and the integral from two to five is

00:07:15.699 --> 00:07:16.000
four.

00:07:16.763 --> 00:07:18.915
But the question runs from five down to

00:07:18.955 --> 00:07:20.404
two, so the sign flips.

00:07:21.028 --> 00:07:22.634
The answer is minus four.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:24.454
Four is wrong.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.476
It forgets that the limits are reversed.

00:07:28.228 --> 00:07:30.472
So keep F of a in brackets,

00:07:31.114 --> 00:07:32.637
flip the sign when the limits swap,

00:07:33.179 --> 00:07:34.842
and add the pieces at a split.

00:07:35.645 --> 00:07:37.892
But a signed integral can surprise you.

00:07:38.655 --> 00:07:41.322
The integral of sine x, from zero to

00:07:41.383 --> 00:07:42.826
two pi, is zero.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:46.025
The arch below the axis cancels the arch

00:07:46.086 --> 00:07:46.367
above.

00:07:47.153 --> 00:07:49.782
Yet the shaded region clearly isn't nothing.

00:07:50.506 --> 00:07:51.742
So what's its area?

00:07:54.368 --> 00:07:55.170
Here are the key notes.

00:07:55.814 --> 00:07:57.541
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:57.603 --> 00:07:58.084
to copy them.
